{% extends "base.html.twig" %}
{% block title %}Waaseyaa: build content applications you control{% endblock %}
{% block head %}<link rel="canonical" href="https://waaseyaa.org/"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Waaseyaa","applicationCategory":"DeveloperApplication","operatingSystem":"Linux, macOS, Windows","programmingLanguage":"PHP","softwareVersion":{{ framework_version|json_encode|raw }},"license":"https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html","codeRepository":"https://github.com/waaseyaa/framework","description":"An open-source PHP framework for content applications."}</script>{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<main id="main">
<section class="hero wrap">

<div class="hero-grid"><h1>Build content<br>applications<br><em>you control.</em></h1><div class="hero-aside"><p>Your content. Your infrastructure.<br>Your way forward.</p><p class="muted">An open-source PHP framework for structured content, publishing workflows, and AI-assisted tools.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/build">Start building </a><a class="text-link" href="#demo">See it in action </a></div><div class="hero-meta"><span>PHP 8.5</span><span>Open source</span><span>Self-hosted</span></div></div></div>
</section>
<section class="demo-section wrap" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-heading">
<div class="section-label"><span id="demo-heading">EXAMPLE APPLICATION</span><span>Local simulation · sample content</span></div>
<div class="demo-shell">
<div class="demo-top"><div class="sample-brand"><span class="sample-icon">f.</span><div>Fieldnotes <small>A community journal</small></div></div><div class="segmented" aria-label="Demo view"><button class="active" data-demo="editor" aria-pressed="true">Workspace</button><button data-demo="preview" aria-pressed="false">Public view</button><button data-demo="api" aria-pressed="false">API</button></div><span class="demo-tag">EXAMPLE APPLICATION</span></div>
<div class="demo-content" id="editor-view">
<aside class="app-sidebar"><span class="sidebar-caption">WORKSPACE</span><span class="sidebar-item selected">▤ <b>Stories</b> <small>03</small></span><span class="sidebar-item">◉ <b>People</b> <small>08</small></span><span class="sidebar-item">⊞ <b>Collections</b> <small>02</small></span><div class="app-sidebar-bottom"><span class="avatar">JL</span><div>Jamie Lee<small>Editor · sample role</small></div></div></aside>
<div class="editor-main"><div class="breadcrumb">Stories <span>/</span> Community garden</div><div class="editor-heading"><h2>A little space to grow.</h2><span class="pill" id="story-status">Draft</span></div><p class="editor-intro">A neighbourhood garden, built one Saturday at a time.</p><div class="landscape" aria-label="Abstract illustration of a community garden"><div class="sun"></div><div class="hill hill-one"></div><div class="hill hill-two"></div><div class="garden-lines"></div><span>FIELDNOTES / PLACES WE SHARE</span></div><div class="editor-fields"><div><small>COLLECTION</small><strong>Community stories</strong></div><div><small>AUTHOR</small><strong>Jamie Lee</strong></div><div><small>VISIBILITY</small><strong>Public, after approval</strong></div></div></div>
<aside class="review-panel"><div class="eyebrow">PUBLISHING</div><h3>A clear path<br>from draft to live.</h3><p>Give people room to create, with a review step before the world sees it.</p><ol class="workflow"><li class="done"><span>✓</span><div>Write your story<small>Saved as a draft</small></div></li><li id="review-step"><span>2</span><div>Review the change<small id="review-step-note">An editor approves</small></div></li><li id="publish-step"><span>3</span><div>Publish with confidence<small>Keep a revision history</small></div></li></ol><button class="button primary full" id="review-button">Review &amp; publish </button><p class="micro" id="demo-feedback" aria-live="polite">Try it. This demo stays in your browser.</p><button class="reset-link" id="reset-demo">Reset example</button></aside>
</div>
<div class="public-preview" id="preview-view" hidden><div class="public-masthead"><strong>Fieldnotes.</strong><span>Stories from the places we share.</span></div><div class="public-story"><div><div class="eyebrow" id="preview-state">DRAFT PREVIEW</div><h2>A little space<br>to grow.</h2><p>A neighbourhood garden, built one Saturday at a time. Meet the people turning an empty lot into something everyone can share.</p><div class="byline">By Jamie Lee <span>4 minute read · sample story</span></div></div><div class="landscape"><div class="sun"></div><div class="hill hill-one"></div><div class="hill hill-two"></div><div class="garden-lines"></div></div></div></div>
<div class="api-preview" id="api-view" hidden><div><div class="eyebrow">THE SAME CONTENT, ANOTHER WAY IN</div><h2>Ready for your<br>next interface.</h2><p>This illustrative response shows the same story as structured data. No request is sent.</p><span class="pill">Illustrative API response</span></div><pre><code id="api-output"></code></pre></div>
<div class="demo-bottom"><span><span class="status-dot"></span> One story. Explicit permissions. Multiple interfaces.</span><a href="/build">Explore the learning path </a></div>
</div></section>
<section class="principles wrap"><div class="principles-intro"><div class="eyebrow">BUILT AROUND OWNERSHIP</div><h2>A foundation.<br>With room to grow.</h2><p>Start with the application you need.<br>Keep the freedom to decide what comes next.</p></div><div class="principle"><span class="principle-number">01</span><h3>Content with structure.</h3><p>Give your content a model, relationships, and a life beyond a single page.</p><a href="/build#learn">Explore the content model </a></div><div class="principle"><span class="principle-number">02</span><h3>Control that stays yours.</h3><p>Choose your infrastructure. Make access deliberate. Keep your data portable.</p><a href="#project">Meet the project </a></div><div class="principle"><span class="principle-number">03</span><h3>AI with boundaries.</h3><p>Make useful tools available to agents, with permissions and review built into the workflow.</p><a href="/build#learn">Explore the learning path </a></div></section>
<section class="possibilities wrap" id="possibilities"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">WHAT COULD YOU BUILD?</div><h2>Useful software.<br>For real communities.</h2></div><p>Three starting points for the imagination.<br><span class="muted">Illustrative use cases, not customer case studies.</span></p></div><div class="use-cases"><a class="use-case" href="/build"><div class="case-art journal-art"><span>THE EVERYDAY<br><em>extraordinary.</em></span><i>FIELDNOTES / VOL. 01</i></div><div class="case-info"><span>01 / PUBLISHING</span><h3>A community journal </h3><p>Stories, contributors, and a considered publishing process.</p></div></a><a class="use-case" href="/build#learn"><div class="case-art directory-art"><div class="directory-line"><i>MK</i><span>Maker &amp; craftsperson<small>Arts and culture</small></span></div><div class="directory-line"><i>NG</i><span>Neighbourhood growers<small>Food and community</small></span></div><div class="directory-line"><i>LC</i><span>Learning circle<small>Education</small></span></div></div><div class="case-info"><span>02 / CONNECTION</span><h3>A living directory </h3><p>People, places, and the relationships that connect them.</p></div></a><a class="use-case" href="/build#learn"><div class="case-art knowledge-art"><span class="orbit o1"></span><span class="orbit o2"></span><span class="orbit o3"></span><strong>Knowledge,<br><em>connected.</em></strong></div><div class="case-info"><span>03 / KNOWLEDGE</span><h3>A shared resource library </h3><p>Structured knowledge for people and the tools they use.</p></div></a></div></section>
<section class="proof-section wrap"><div class="eyebrow">VERIFIABLE EXAMPLES</div><h2>This site is the demo</h2><p>Waaseyaa.org is a Waaseyaa application. Its releases, roadmap, and case studies are revisionable entities synced from Markdown in Git. The same content is available as HTML, Markdown, and read-only MCP. Runtime writes are blocked by the site's access policy.</p><p>Explore <a href="/production">the documented applications</a>, including First Nations Procurement Inc. The case studies explain their scope and limits.</p><pre><code>curl -s -H 'Accept: text/markdown' https://waaseyaa.org/releases</code></pre><pre><code>curl -s -X POST https://waaseyaa.org/mcp -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"release_list","arguments":{}}}'</code></pre><p>For organizations evaluating operations and support, read <a href="/why">the project's values</a>, <a href="/compare">the comparison</a>, and <a href="/project">current maturity and support</a>.</p></section><section class="project-section" id="project"><div class="wrap project-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">OPEN BY DESIGN</div><h2>The Waaseyaa<br>project.</h2><p>Waaseyaa is an open-source project. Explore the code, understand the tradeoffs, and help shape what comes next.</p><a class="button light" href="/build">Start building </a></div><div class="project-notes"><article><span>THE FOUNDATION</span><h3>Waaseyaa Framework</h3><p>The reusable engine for content applications. Useful on its own, on infrastructure you choose.</p></article><article><span>THE BUILDER DIRECTION</span><h3>Waaseyaa Studio</h3><p>An open-source builder distribution composing the framework. Availability and verified capabilities will be documented separately.</p></article><div class="release-note"><span class="status-dot"></span><p>Framework is alpha.<br><small>Running {{ framework_version }}. Released {{ release_date }}. <a href="/releases">Release notes</a> and <a href="/roadmap">roadmap</a>.</small></p></div></div></div></section>
</main>
<dialog id="review-dialog"><form method="dialog"><button class="dialog-close" aria-label="Close review">×</button></form><div class="eyebrow">LOCAL PUBLISHING SIMULATION</div><h2>One last look.</h2><p>You’re reviewing <strong>A little space to grow.</strong> The sample story will become visible in this demo’s public view.</p><div class="change-summary"><span>Story status</span><strong>Draft to published</strong><span>Audience</span><strong>Public</strong><span>Reviewer</span><strong>Jamie Lee · sample editor</strong></div><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="review-check"> I’ve reviewed this sample story.</label><p class="form-error" id="review-error" aria-live="polite"></p><button class="button primary full" id="confirm-publish">Publish in demo </button><p class="micro">Local simulation. Nothing is sent or published online.</p></dialog>
{% endblock %}
